class Solution {
    public ArrayList<ArrayList<Integer>> levelOrder(Node root) {

        ArrayList<ArrayList<Integer>> list = new ArrayList<>();               // Initialize result list of lists
        if(root == null){ return list; }                                      // Base case: empty tree

        Queue<Node> q = new LinkedList<>();                                   // Queue for BFS traversal

        q.add(root);                                                          // Enqueue root node
        
        ArrayList<Integer> level = new ArrayList<>();                         // List to store current level nodes

        while(!q.isEmpty()){                                                  // Process until queue empty
            int size = q.size();                                              // Number of nodes at current level
            level = new ArrayList<>();                                        // Create new level list
            
            for(int i=0;i<size;i++){                                          // Process all nodes at current level
                Node cur = q.remove();                                        // Dequeue current node
                level.add(cur.data);                                          // Add current node data to level list
        
                if(cur.left != null){ q.add(cur.left); }                      // Enqueue left child if exists
                if(cur.right != null){ q.add(cur.right); }                    // Enqueue right child if exists
            }
            list.add(level);                                                  // Add completed level to result
        }
        return list;                                                          // Return level order traversal
    }
}

//////////////////////// DRY RUN /////////////////////////////

Example: root = [10, 20, 30, 40, 60]

       10
      /  \
     20   30
    / \ 
   40  60

Iteration 1: size=1, level=[10], add 20, 30 → list=[[10]]
Iteration 2: size=2, level=[20,30], add 40, 60 → list=[[10],[20,30]]
Iteration 3: size=2, level=[40,60], add nothing → list=[[10],[20,30],[40,60]]

Output: [[10], [20, 30], [40, 60]]

//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Level Order Line by Line
Given root of a binary tree, return its level order traversal with each level in a separate list.

Examples:
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Input: root = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, N, N, N, N, N, 8]

        1
       / \
      2   3
     / \ / \
    4  5 6  7
            \
             8

Output: [[1], [2, 3], [4, 5, 6, 7], [8]]
Explanation: Level 0: [1], Level 1: [2,3], Level 2: [4,5,6,7], Level 3: [8]

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Input: root = [10, 20, 30, 40, 60]

       10
      /  \
     20   30
    / \ 
   40  60

Output: [[10], [20, 30], [40, 60]]
Explanation: Level 0: [10], Level 1: [20,30], Level 2: [40,60]

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Constraints:
• 1 ≤ number of nodes ≤ 1000
• 0 ≤ node->data ≤ 100

